// `reflect` mirrors about a **unit** normal, which an integer vector cannot carry — the same reason
// `normalize` refuses one. The refusal names the requirement rather than answering with a rounded
// direction, so a program cannot mistake a truncated reflection for the real one.
// expect: error E0007 at 11:6
// expect: exit 1
use std.{vec}

@packed struct IVec3 { x: i32; y: i32; z: i32 }
impl vec.Kernels for IVec3 {}

echo IVec3 { x: 1i32, y: 2i32, z: 3i32 }.reflect(IVec3 { x: 0i32, y: 1i32, z: 0i32 })
